From d73ea42de292973770e52ff901460d059ccdb4a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 02:59:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Config: hypre on the host with a device on the GPU
 (--hypre-on-host)

The option `--hypre-on-host` (or `-hoh`, `--no-hypre-on-host` and
`-no-hoh` cancelling it), declared by declareDefaultOptions, or else the
environment variable MFEM_MGIS_HYPRE_ON_HOST, makes hypre allocate its
memory and compute on the host while the device of MFEM uses a GPU: the
behaviours and the computations of MFEM and of mfem-mgis stay on the
device, and MFEM gives the data of hypre on the host
(mfem::HypreUsingGPU is false). This is faster for small linear
systems, whose resolutions on a GPU are dominated by the launches of
kernels. initialize prevents the configuration of the device from making
hypre use the GPU (mfem::Hypre::configure_runtime_policy_from_mfem) and
sets the policy of hypre to the host after it. The size of the pool of
memory of hypre on the GPU (--hypre-device-pool-size) is then refused.

Tests: DeviceOptionTest checks where hypre computes (--expected-hypre)
and an expected error of the initialization (--expected-error), with
four new variants on the GPU (option, environment variable, option
cancelling the variable, refusal of the pool size);
HypreILUTestP-cuda-hypre-on-host and
BatchIntegrationTestP-cuda-hypre-on-host (behaviours and kernels on the
GPU, hypre on the host). Removing both settings makes the tests fail.
---
