 include/MFEMMGIS/Config.hxx                   | 12 +++
 src/Config.cxx                                | 91 +++++++++++++++++++
 tests/CMakeLists.txt                          | 46 +++++++++-
 tests/DeviceOptionTest.cxx                    | 60 +++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 215 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
index e3575c523c..2bd854b512 100644
--- a/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
+++ b/docs/source/user_guide/batch_computations.rst
@@ -542,6 +542,17 @@ before the first allocation of :code:`hypre` on the GPU. If :code:`hypre`
 does not use a pool of :code:`Umpire` on the GPU, the option is refused,
 and the environment variable is ignored with a warning.
 
+For small linear systems, whose resolutions on a GPU are dominated by the
+launches of kernels, :code:`hypre` may compute on the host while the
+behaviours and the computations of :code:`MFEM` and of :code:`mfem-mgis`
+stay on the GPU: option :code:`--hypre-on-host` (or :code:`-hoh`, and
+:code:`--no-hypre-on-host` to cancel it), declared by
+:code:`mfem_mgis::declareDefaultOptions`, or environment variable
+:code:`MFEM_MGIS_HYPRE_ON_HOST`. :code:`MFEM` then copies the matrices and
+the vectors given to :code:`hypre` on the host, and
+:code:`mfem::HypreUsingGPU` is false: the restrictions listed above do not
+apply.
+
 .. _mfem_mgis_batch_computations_amgx:
 
 AmgX
